meta {
  name: 12. Add Same UPI for Second Driver (BUG-178, expect rejected)
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/vpas
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "vpa": "{{driverVpa}}",
    "driverId": "{{secondDriverId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.success: eq false
  res.body.statusCode: eq 400
  res.body.message: eq This UPI is already linked to another driver. Contact support.
}

docs {
  BUG-178 / MBT-178. Before the fix, `VPAService.createVPAForDriver` handed an existing,
  unattached UPI to whichever driver asked for it next — driver A (step 10's owner) would
  silently lose {{driverVpa}} (and their default payout method with it) the moment the second
  driver added the same UPI, and the row was force-marked ACTIVE/VERIFIED for the new driver
  without any verification or name match.

  Fixed in plutus-java `VPAService.createVPAForDriver` /
  `isClaimedByAnotherDriver` (branch `fix/BUG-178-vpa-driver-remapping`, not
  yet on staging as of 2026-09-28): a UPI already held by a *different*, non-DEACTIVATED driver
  now throws `BadRequestException("This UPI is already linked to another driver. Contact
  support.")`.

  `POST /api/vpas` (`VPAResource.createVPA`) doesn't catch this exception itself, so it falls
  through to `GenericExceptionMapper`, which turns it into `CommonResponse.error(message, 400)` —
  then `ApiResponseFilter` rewrites the wire status from 400 to 200 (see `folder.bru`), which is
  why `res.status: eq 200` is correct here even though this is the failure case.

  Same fix (same exact message) also applies to `POST /api/vpas/without-verification`, the
  verify/fetch lookup (`POST /api/vpas/verify/{vpaNumber}?driverId=`, which returns the message
  as a bare string wrapped by `ApiResponseFilter` into `data` *and* `message` rather than through
  the `CommonResponse` from `GenericExceptionMapper`), and `POST /api/vpas/attach/{id}?driverId=`
  — not separately exercised here.

  Step 13 checks driver A's list to confirm {{driverVpa}} wasn't actually moved.
}
